    <keyword>SET BELL command</keyword>
  </keywords>
  <body>
    <header>
      <para styleclass="Heading1">SET BELL Command</para>
    </header>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><snippet src="__FoxProOnly" inline="false"/></para>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><snippet src="__CommandInclude" inline="false"/></para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Purpose</para>
    <para styleclass="Normal">Enables or disables the bell that sounds when the user fills a field in a full-screen input, or enters invalid data.</para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Syntax</para>
    <para styleclass="Code with box">SET BELL ON | OFF | &amp;&lt;cMacro&gt;<br/>SET BELL TO [&lt;Options&gt;]</para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Arguments</para>
    <para styleclass="List">ON | OFF<tab />Enables or disables the bell. The value may also be a macro (&amp;) that evaluates to ON or OFF.</para>
    <para styleclass="List">TO [&lt;Options&gt;]<tab />In Visual FoxPro this sets the frequency and duration of the bell. The command is accepted but ignored.</para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Remarks</para>
    <para styleclass="Normal">The setting is also available with the function <link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="html\Overload_XSharp_Core_Functions_SetBeep.htm" domain="XSharpRef.chm">SetBeep()</link>.</para>
    <para styleclass="Body Text"><snippet src="__IncludeLibVFP" inline="false"/></para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">See Also</para>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="command_SET_CONFIRM">SET CONFIRM</link>, <link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="html\Overload_XSharp_Core_Functions_SetBeep.htm" domain="XSharpRef.chm">SetBeep()</link></para>
  </body>
